// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// NETHERLANDS — Smartious city-level + country-level data
// Live online Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, Pearson Edexcel, IB Diploma,
// and American AP for expat, international, and Dutch families across
// Amsterdam, The Hague, Rotterdam, Utrecht, Eindhoven, and Groningen.
//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING. THIS PAGE SITS IN THE
// STRICTEST HONESTY TIER (with France and Sweden), AND THE LAW IS IN
// ACTIVE FLUX AS OF MID-2026:
// There is NO home-education right in Dutch law. Leerplicht runs from
// age 5 through the school year the child turns 16 and is met by
// enrolment at a recognised school; kwalificatieplicht then runs to 18
// (until a startkwalificatie). An unrecognised foreign online school
// does NOT satisfy leerplicht.
//
// The one relevant exemption is Article 5 onder b Leerplichtwet 1969:
// exemption from the duty to enrol where parents hold overwegende
// bedenkingen (overriding objections) against the RICHTING — the
// religious or philosophical direction — of every school within
// reasonable distance, notified to the municipality under Arts. 6/8.
// Usage grew from 575 children (2013-14) to about 2,860 (2024-25),
// currently without inspection. CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:
// (1) the exemption is essentially unavailable once a child has been
//     enrolled at a school of that direction;
// (2) the Hoge Raad ruling of 21 April 2026 TIGHTENED the framework —
//     objections against public (openbaar) education can succeed only
//     in exceptional cases;
// (3) the OM, having suspended prosecutions in April 2025, has
//     announced it will RESUME criminal enforcement following that
//     ruling, and a legislative proposal would add a compulsory
//     home-education plan and quality supervision.
// NEVER present 5b as a route Smartious enables, advises on, or
// benefits from. State it factually, note the flux, refer families to
// a Dutch education lawyer. We serve families who already lawfully
// hold an exemption without making any claims about obtaining one.
//
// NO POST-16 FREE WINDOW: unlike Sweden, kwalificatieplicht (16-18)
// continues after leerplicht. How it applies to internationally
// educated teenagers is a question for the leerplichtambtenaar or a
// lawyer — never claim an A-Level route satisfies it.
//
// CORE POSITIONING, in order: (1) supplementary alongside a school
// enrolment — the main Dutch use case; (2) the international-school
// population (waitlists at the subsidised Dutch International Schools,
// EUR 20,000-30,000 at the private internationals); (3) structured
// curriculum for families who already lawfully hold a 5b exemption.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

